[[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/2874931802","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/1904#issuecomment-2874931802","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/1904","id":2874931802,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs6rW_pa","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T03:07:50Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T06:54:36Z","body":"Thanks for the sandbox @benjavicente, I've been testing a bunch of similar field validation setups \n\nIt may be possible to use [`Field.Validity`](https://base-ui.com/react/components/field#validity) instead of `Field.Error` to achieve this, it accepts a function child with the validity state as an arg, though I haven't tested this myself\n\nFor Field.Error if you also consider how the errors are cleared/revalidated, I've found that the UX feels better when using only the native validation for required, and doing everything else in the validate function, that way you have more control over the order and timing of all the checks","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"rea